id: pm-1wujzi
title: "Occupancy is a per-item history fold with no collection surface: reading which items a fleet holds costs one full history-stream read per item, while the three lifecycle statuses that are filterable are empty across all 2,245 items"
description: "claim_state is derived by resolveClaimStateContext (src/sdk/query/get.ts:159) folding readHistoryEntries over one item's stream, and it is reachable only from pm get. No collection surface filters or projects it: pm list publishes 69 flags and none is claim-aware, and --full returns 25 field keys without claim_state. The queryable ownership vocabulary is --assignee over a mutable metadata field that 288 items carry and that cannot distinguish a live claim from a released one. Meanwhile draft, in_progress and blocked are 0 across all 2,245 items, so pm list-in-progress and pm list-blocked are structurally empty. Answering 'what does the fleet hold right now' therefore costs 2,258 stream folds over 42,771 entries on this corpus, and O(corpus) stream reads at the million-item target. Duplicate check: searched claim/owner/fleet/who-is-working lineages and read pm-ugld, pm-lvyd, pm-0mhspz, pm-3oqjnc, pm-tch9cs, pm-ydshl9, pm-801d; none owns bulk occupancy readability."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",concurrency,scale
created_at: "2026-08-01T09:46:07.928Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-01T09:58:10.235Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 900
acceptance_criteria: Collection reads filter and project occupancy without one history fold per item; occupancy is served from maintained derived state; an occupancy-interval read returns claim intervals with holder identity and mutation-during-hold; fleet-wide occupancy query cost is independent of history length; pm-4k6b entry (24) peer-conditioning and pm-3oqjnc allocation both consume the same surface
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make live and historical occupancy readable in bulk so fleet algorithms have the input they already assume
value: Thousands of concurrent agents can see the work-front without O(corpus x stream) reads; contention and abandonment become queryable signals
why_now: pm-4k6b entry (24) and pm-3oqjnc are both specified against a claim ledger that is assumed readable and is not; each would rediscover this independently
